    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d409">

                <pb facs="0740" n="636" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg636"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt
                    Papers</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Communiqué: Second Draft</hi></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                        calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1943-12-02T23:59:59+03:25"
                        notBefore="1943-12-01T00:00:00+03:25">undated</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Editorial Note.</hi>—As in the case of the first
                    draft, this was apparently an American paper. No evidence has been found of its
                    being considered outside the American Delegation.</p>
                <p>The handwritten changes or corrections (indicated typographically as in the first
                    draft, printed <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>) appear to be wholly or in
                    part in Roosevelt’s handwriting; possibly
                    some are Hopkins’. Some of the changes
                    made on this draft were not incorporated in the typewritten text of the third
                    draft (printed <hi rendition="#italic">infra</hi>). From this, it may be
                    surmised that such changes were written in on this draft—possibly by Hopkins—at the same time they were written in
                    on the third draft by Roosevelt.]</p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Second Draft</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d409-f1"/></p>
                <p>WE<anchor n="2" xml:id="d409-f2"/>—The President of the United States, The Prime
                    Minister of Great Britain, and The Premier of Soviet Russia, Marshal of the Red
                    Army, have met these four days past, in this city of Teheran, <del
                        rendition="#strikethrough">and</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">have</del>
                    <pb facs="0741" n="637" xml:id="pg637"/>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">bent</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">our</del><anchor n="3" xml:id="d409-f3"/>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">united</del> efforts toward solutions of
                        our<anchor n="4" xml:id="d409-f4"/> military and political problems.<anchor
                        n="5" xml:id="d409-f5"/></p>
                <p>We express our determination that our nations shall work together in war and in
                    the peace that will follow.</p>
                <p>As to war—our military staffs have joined in our round table discussions, and we
                    have concerted our plans for the <del rendition="#strikethrough">final</del>
                    destruction of the German forces. We have reached complete agreement as to the
                    scope and timing of the operations <del rendition="#strikethrough">which</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">will</del>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to</hi> be undertaken from the East, West and South,
                        <del rendition="#strikethrough">and</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">arrangements</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">were</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">made</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">to</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">ensure</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">intimate</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">and</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">continuous</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">cooperation.</del></p>
                <p><del rendition="#strikethrough">The</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">road</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">is</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">still</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">bloody</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">and</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">hard</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">and</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">long.</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">But</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">t</del><hi rendition="#italic">T</hi>he common
                    understanding which we have here reached guarantees that victory will be
                    ours.</p>
                <p>And as to peace—our<anchor n="6" xml:id="d409-f6"/>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">mutual</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">belief</del><anchor n="7" xml:id="d409-f7"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">we are confident that</hi>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">it</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">will</del>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">our</hi> concord <del rendition="#strikethrough"
                        >gives</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">us</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">courage</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">to</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">hope</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">that</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">we</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">may</del>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">will</hi> make it endure. We recognize fully <del
                        rendition="#strikethrough">our</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">great</del>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">the supreme</hi> responsibilit<del
                        rendition="#strikethrough">ies</del><hi rendition="#italic">y</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">resting upon us &amp; all the United Nations</hi> to
                        <del rendition="#strikethrough">help</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">in</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">the</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">determination</del>
                    <hi rendition="#italic"><del rendition="#strikethrough">making</del>
                        <del rendition="#strikethrough">of</del> make</hi> a peace which will <del
                        rendition="#strikethrough">meet</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">approval</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">of</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">the</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">greater</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">part</del>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">command the good will of the overwhelming mass</hi> of
                    the peoples of the world, and<anchor n="8" xml:id="d409-f8"/>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">ensure</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">a</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">lasting</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">surcease</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">from</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">war</del>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">banish the scourge &amp; terror of war for many
                        generations.</hi></p>
                <p>With our diplomatic advisors we have surveyed the problems of the future. We
                    shall seek the cooperation and the active participation of all nations, large
                    and small, whose peoples in heart and mind are dedicated, as are our own
                    peoples, to the elimination of tyranny and slavery, oppression and intolerance.
                    We will welcome them, as they may choose to come, into a world family of<anchor
                        n="9" xml:id="d409-f9"/> democratic nations.</p>
                <p>No power on earth can prevent our destroying the German armies by land, their
                        <del rendition="#strikethrough">submarines</del>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">U boats</hi> by sea,
                    and their war plants <hi rendition="#italic"><del rendition="#strikethrough"
                            >&amp;</del>
                        <del rendition="#strikethrough">armies</del></hi> from the air.</p>
                <p>Our attack will be relentless <hi rendition="#italic">&amp; increasing</hi>.</p>
                <p>Emerging from these <hi rendition="#italic">cordial</hi> conferences we look with
                    confidence toward the day when all peoples of the world may live free lives,
                    untouched <pb facs="0742" n="638" xml:id="pg638"/> by tyranny, and according to
                    their varying desires and their own consciences.</p>
                <p>We came here with hope and determination. We leave here, friends in fact, in
                    spirit <del rendition="#strikethrough">as</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">well</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">as</del>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;</hi> in purpose.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">And</hi>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">And</del> we shall meet again as the war—and the
                    peace—progresses!</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d409-f1" n="1" xml:id="d409-f1-content">
                <p>In the upper left-hand corner of this draft appears the handwritten date
                    “12/2/43”, presumably associated with the procedural note of December 2, 1943,
                    referred to in the editorial note to the first draft, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >supra.</hi></p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d409-f2" n="2" xml:id="d409-f2-content">
                <p>This word was underlined by hand.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d409-f3" n="3" xml:id="d409-f3-content">
                <p>Over the word “our” was written the word “their”, which, in turn, was crossed
                    out.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d409-f4" n="4" xml:id="d409-f4-content">
                <p>The word “our” was crossed out, and the word “their” was written above it. The
                    word “their” was then crossed out, and the word “our” was written below the
                    deleted typewritten “our”.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d409-f5" n="5" xml:id="d409-f5-content">
                <p>After the word “problems” was written “of the three great allies”, and these
                    words were crossed out. In the left-hand margin, apparently as a substitution
                    for the portion of the sentence following the word “Teheran,” were written the
                    following words: “&amp; have shaped &amp; <del rendition="#strikethrough"
                        >formed</del>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">confirmed</hi> our united policy. <del
                        rendition="#strikethrough">for</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">the</del>
                    <del rendition="#strikethrough">future</del>.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d409-f6" n="6" xml:id="d409-f6-content">
                <p>The word “our” was presumably intended to be crossed out.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d409-f7" n="7" xml:id="d409-f7-content">
                <p>The words “mutual belief” were struck over with typewritten “x’s”.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d409-f8" n="8" xml:id="d409-f8-content">
                <p>The word “and” was presumably intended to be crossed out.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d409-f9" n="9" xml:id="d409-f9-content">
                <p>After the word “of” appears an undecipherable typewritten word of five letters
                    which was struck over with typewritten “x’s”.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
